Before we prove \pref{lem:balancededgesimproved}, we need the following lemma.

\begin{lemma}  \label{lem:incident}
    Let $G \sim \calG_{n,m}$. Suppose that $\beta \geq \beta^*$. With probability $1-n^{-\omega(1)}$, for any $T\subseteq V$, $|T|= \beta n$, the number of edges incident to $T$ is at least least $c \beta n / 40$.
\end{lemma}

Now we prove this lemma.

For any vertex $v\in V$, its expected degree in $\calG_{n, m}$ is $2c$. We would like to prove that the probability that the degree is at most $c/10$ is very low. Indeed, we claim a more general statement.

